<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farrukh Yasar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1500">1500</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Farrukh Yasar was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shirvanshah">Shirvanshah</a> from the 1460s until 1500, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamakhi">Shamakhi</a> as an ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a>. In 1488, with Aq Qoyunlu help, his forces defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaykh-haydar">Shaykh Haydar</a>, leader of the militant Safavid order, who had invaded Shirvan. In 1500 Haydar's son Ismail, the future Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a>, defeated and killed him in revenge.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farrukh-yasar.jpg" alt="Farrukh Yasar" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gulustan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A4%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%80%D1%83%D1%85_%D0%AF%D1%81%D0%B0%D1%80.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
